# ── THE DISMISSAL THAT MUST NOT BE ALLOWED TO GO QUIET ───────────────────────
#
# Dependabot alert #15 (GHSA-x2fc-mxcx-w4mf, high, `mathjs` prototype pollution
# via deepExtend on configuration update) rides on `quantum-circuit`, which the
# maintainer has ruled STAYS: it is a declared `role=second-oracle` cross-verify
# oracle, and that standing outweighs an alert count.
#
# MEASURED 2026-09-09, npm registry: quantum-circuit has 240 published releases;
# `latest` is 0.9.250; the declared `mathjs` range across ALL 240 is one of
# ^3.8.0 / ^3.20.2 / ^6.0.3 / ^6.6.5, so the highest major any release has EVER
# admitted is 6. The advisory's first patched version is 7.5.1. There is
# therefore no version fix — not today, and not in any release ever published.
#
# The dismissal's premise is enforced offline by
# `src/Core.TypeScript/hygiene/lint-mathjs-dismissal-premise.ts`. What that lint
# CANNOT see is upstream changing its mind, so the expiry is this row: when
# quantum-circuit's latest release declares a mathjs range admitting 7.x, the
# resolver returns FIX-AVAILABLE, --report says `moved`, and the dismissal gets
# revisited rather than aging into a permanent silence.
#
# ref grammar: npm:<package>!<dependency>@<first-patched-major>
